 "text": "Hey, good to have you back. How are you? That's lot of paper. I assume she keeps them in boxes or folders. Look for patterns. One side only. That's a telling sign. If she reads one story and the next one is gone, don't touch the box. Go through the entire collection, one letter each. Then you list everything she has and where it is, including the dull stuff. Most times a simple list like that changes the number. A photo is much bigger. Ask yourself if you'd buy ticket now or keep waiting.",
